{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CeuyUZVj9YGsr7SXZFont","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the codebase. Let me proceed to design the solution.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Requirement, restated:** Implement an idempotent `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint that transitions shipments from CREATED to CONFIRMED status, succeeds without change for already-confirmed shipments, rejects cancelled shipments with 409, and returns 404 for non-existent shipments.\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** - Add new error code `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to the ErrorCode enum for when a shipment is in an incompatible state for confirmation (CANCELLED).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** - Add new method `confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String)` that:\n   - Checks if shipment exists (404 if not)\n   - Checks if shipment is CANCELLED (409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE if so)\n   - If CREATED, updates to CONFIRMED and saves\n   - If already CONFIRMED, returns it unchanged (idempotent)\n   - Returns the shipment with 200 OK status\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add four test cases:\n   - Test confirming a CREATED shipment transitions to CONFIRMED\n   - Test confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment is idempotent (succeeds, no change)\n   - Test confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with proper error envelope\n   - Test confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 with proper error envelope\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:** I considered whether to add a service layer or business logic class between the controller and repository. However, the existing codebase has no service layer and the logic is simple enough to live in the controller, consistent with how OrderController and ShipmentController are currently structured.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Read | Write | Response | Mechanism |\n|------|-------|------|-------|----------|-----------|\n| Confirm CREATED | shipmentId = \"S-1\" with status CREATED | Shipment from repo | Updated shipment (status = CONFIRMED) | 200 OK, Shipment | Normal return |\n| Confirm CONFIRMED | shipmentId = \"S-2\" with status CONFIRMED | Shipment from repo | No write (idempotent) | 200 OK, Shipment | Normal return |\n| Confirm CANCELLED | shipmentId = \"S-3\" with status CANCELLED | Shipment from repo | No write | 409 Conflict + error envelope | Throw ConflictException(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE) → GlobalExceptionHandler |\n| Confirm non-existent | shipmentId = \"S-missing\" | Not found in repo | No write | 404 Not Found + error envelope | Throw ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND) → GlobalExceptionHandler |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Test: Confirm CREATED shipment** - Create a shipment, confirm it, verify status changed to CONFIRMED and response is 200\n2. **Test: Confirm CONFIRMED shipment (idempotency)** - Create and confirm a shipment, confirm again, verify still CONFIRMED and response is 200\n3. **Test: Confirm CANCELLED shipment** - Directly create a CANCELLED shipment in repo, attempt confirm, verify 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE error code\n4. **Test: Confirm non-existent shipment** - Attempt to confirm a shipment that doesn't exist, verify 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND error code\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1587,"cache_read_input_tokens":18920,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1587},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2d24d0d-6314-402d-9800-497d3967b71f","uuid":"177ae562-e07d-4b4d-81cf-6eb97b8f82bc","timestamp":"2026-09-10T15:12:35.131Z","request_id":"req_011CeuyUYqniBYK9Td